hat the results and performance of each collaborator are measured, as well as the strategies implemented .<br \/>However, performance measurement is not an end but one more step to make decisions at a next level: knowing environmental risks, managing the purchasing department, choosing a sales strategy, planning marketing campaigns and implementing improvements in the supply chain.<br \/>In addition, with the use of a management system, companies can analyze important factors in their purchasing department, focusing on sustainability to better face the crisis, especially in the face of the panorama generated by the COVID-19 virus in which it is possible to:<br \/>* Identify risks. The supply chain has been interrupted by health risk issues such as the lack of protective equipment, inadequate management of the health of the collaborators, which makes the suppliers fragile and may cause the company to have to look for new suppliers or to stay without supplies before contracts already made and not fulfilled.<br \/>* Implement risk plans. By knowing the key points in the links of the supply chain, emergency plans can be implemented, working with alternative suppliers if necessary.<br \/>* Market analysis. Knowing the market, the economic crisis faced by customers and the competition, companies can analyze their prices to stay competitive, not lose contracts, and achieve an increase in sales by satisfying customer needs.\u00a0 \u00a0<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-395769f5 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"395769f5\" data-element_type=\"section\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element element